    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just more fighting against the inevitable, isn't it? just dragging out the misery for a few more years. if the end result is always going to be the same because it’s baked into my blood, isn't \"managing\" it just a way to prolong the inevitable suffering? it feels like i'm just fighting a losing battle against my own existence.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a very real and painful perspective to feel like any effort is merely prolonging suffering. Perhaps the focus doesn't need to be on \"winning\" against destiny, but rather on finding pockets of meaning *alongside* the challenges. Allowing yourself to experience present moments—even small ones—can sometimes shift the focus from the ultimate endpoint to the reality of the now. Reaching out to support groups focused on shared life experiences, rather than just clinical management, might offer a community understanding of this burden.",
      "source": "target",
